Lets the core keep the page a switch leaves over the one it shows until that one has drawn (issue
#1438). On the Mac, a page shown again gets a new compositor, and its view shows only its
background colour until that compositor's first frame, 60 to 230 ms on GitHub's hosted Mac, so the
window showed no page partway through every tab and Space switch. A hook only: the core decides
what stays, through content::CallWhenFrameShown.

